# Source-First

Before using an external API or library pattern:

1. Check `repos/github.com/<owner>/<repo>` for a local mirror.
2. If missing, run `node scripts/opensource.mjs <url>` or `node scripts/sync-sources.mjs`.
3. Read the actual source — types, tests, examples — not docs alone.
4. For huge monorepos, use Repomix or yek (see `playbooks/workflow.md`).

## Context dumps

```bash
npx repomix --output context.txt          # normal repos
npx yek --dirs src --output context.txt   # huge monorepos
```

## Reference projects

For features modeled on a production app, index and read Graphify first:

```bash
node scripts/index-reference.mjs <name>
# Read references/<name>/.graphify/GRAPH_REPORT.md
```
